<title>AUSTRALIA: Macquarie Bank shares jump on result.</title>
<headline>Macquarie Bank shares jump on result.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in investment bank Macquarie Bank Ltd jumped 14 cents to A$9.60 on Monday, equal to their record high, after the bank reported a 25.5 percent rise in full year net profit to A$116.94 million.</p>
<p>Combined with a final dividend of 25 cents per share, the result bettered market expectations.</p>
<p>&quot;It was a pretty strong result,&quot; one dealer said, noting a strong that shareholder's return.</p>
<p>By 11.10 a.m. (0110 GMT), Macquarie Bank shares had eased to be eight cents higher at A$9.54 on turnover of 270,409 shares.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
